# CodeQL's in-source suppressions, which security-and-quality doesn't run: codeql.yml runs them beside it, so a result
# under one is marked suppressed in the SARIF (and the gate after the analysis lets it through). One line: it ends in
# "// lgtm[java/rule] why". One member: @SuppressWarnings("lgtm[java/rule]") // why. SuppressionsHaveReasonsTest
# makes each say why; a whole rule left out goes in a config file's query-filters, each with its reason
# (WorkflowRulesTest).
- query: AlertSuppression.ql
  from: codeql/java-queries
- query: AlertSuppressionAnnotations.ql
  from: codeql/java-queries
